- so allowing location simple gives us lattitute longitude and lets us know their exact location? 
	Yes. With permission, the browser sends latitude/longitude for the device's current position; the app saves those coordinates for a new report and makes report coordinates public. They are approximate, not guaranteed exact: the browser also reports an accuracy radius with 95% confidence. Geolocation requires HTTPS and explicit permission. See [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/GeolocationCoordinates/accuracy) and [MDN Geolocation](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Geolocation/getCurrentPosition).
